# Uploads (Multer + Sharp)

Use `src/utils/multer.js` only — do not add ad-hoc multer configs in routers.

## Prefer presets

```js
import { imageUpload, fileUpload, UPLOAD_PRESETS, pdfUpload } from "../../utils/multer.js";

...imageUpload(UPLOAD_PRESETS.avatar({ folder: "users" }))
...imageUpload(UPLOAD_PRESETS.gallery({ folder: "products", maxCount: 8 }))
...fileUpload(UPLOAD_PRESETS.pdf({ folder: "tickets" }))
...spreadsheetUpload({ folder: "imports" })
```

## Custom image config

```js
...imageUpload({
  folder: "custom",
  fields: "image",          // string | string[] | { name, maxCount }[]
  maxCount: 1,
  generateLQIP: true,
  lqipAsFile: false,
  compressOptions: { quality: 85, maxWidth: 1600, format: "jpeg" },
  fileFilter: "image",      // or FILE_KINDS key / custom { allowedMimeTypes, allowedExtensions }
  limits: { fileSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024 },
})
```

## Controllers

```js
const { path, lqip } = getSingleImage(req, "image");
const { paths, lqips } = getMultipleImages(req, "images");
```

## Security (keep these)

- Random disk names (`nanoid`) — never trust client filenames on disk.
- Reject SVG/HTML/executable MIME.
- Magic-byte validation after upload.
- Relative paths under `/uploads/...` only in API responses.
